    why: "Managers are rewarded for beating budget, and repairs are the easiest line to cut quietly. The warning signs show up elsewhere: open work orders piling up, longer unit turn times, more tenant complaints, lower renewal rates and a building that looks tired on your site visits. Compare the underspend with the work-order log and the preventive maintenance schedule. A favorable variance is good news only if the work was done more cheaply, not skipped.",
