    why: "The metrics follow the leases. Apartment leases turn over every year or so, so the key numbers move fast: how many units are filled, at what rents and whether residents pay and stay. Office leases last years, so performance is lumpy: what matters is how much income is at risk soon, how many prospects are in the pipeline and what each deal costs after concessions. NOI against budget is the result; the KPIs are the leading indicators that explain and predict it.",
    trap: "The follow-up: which are the best leading indicators? For apartments, leasing traffic and renewals on upcoming expiries; for office, tours and proposals in the pipeline, months before any lease is signed.",
