    why: "The categories answer different questions. Life-safety asks what you must do: skipping it risks injury, fines, insurance problems and a loan default. Maintenance asks what keeps the building working and competitive at the lowest lifetime cost: a roof replaced on schedule is cheaper than one that fails and damages tenant space. ROI capex asks whether spending creates more value than it costs, judged on return on cost against the exit cap rate. Tag every project, so a nice-to-have lobby can't hide under maintenance.",
