    why: "Coinsurance stops owners from insuring a fraction of the building, paying a fraction of the premium and still collecting in full on the partial losses that make up most claims. Values drift below the requirement without anyone deciding to underinsure, because construction costs can rise faster than owners update their schedules. Many policies waive coinsurance through an agreed-value endorsement, which relies on a current, signed statement of values. Lenders check coverage against replacement cost for the same reason.",
