    why: "A sale is the last chance to capture the value the business plan created, and much of the price is decided before bids arrive. Preparation removes reasons for buyers to discount: an unexplained expense reconciliation, missing estoppels or a known roof problem all become price cuts. Opinions of value help choose the broker, but the highest estimate doesn't make the best broker. Choosing the buyer is a risk decision: a slightly lower bid with a large hard deposit and no financing contingency often beats the top number.",
    trap: "The follow-up: when would you skip a broad auction? When the buyer pool is small or one buyer, such as a partner or a neighbor, will pay full value. A targeted sale is faster and quieter but gives up competitive tension.",
